% SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
% =====================================================================
% fixtures.clausal -- representative profiles for ch/swiss_fadp_s4_criminal_provisions.
% A TOP-LAYER consumer: it imports the slice's PUBLIC predicate it calls.
% Profile keys and subject ids are atoms and need no import.
%
% A profile is an ATTRIBUTE LIST [attribute(Key, Value), ...] (the order's
% typed input contract). Every route has a positive case and a one-unit
% near-miss control:
%   DSG Art 63 / 62(2) / 61(a) / 60(1)(b)(1)  punishable vs one element false
%   DSG Arts 61, 60(2) complaint              filed vs missing; ex officio
%   DSG Art 64(2) boundary                    50000 francs vs 50001 francs
%   GDPR Art 83(5)                            established vs unsure
%   comparison                                same vs differs
%   referral                                  unsure conduct vs conduct met
%   input check                               duplicate key vs single key
% The limitation dates (DSG Art 66) are query arguments, not profile keys:
% the public-interface tests pass them directly.
% =====================================================================

:- module(fixtures, [
    swiss_fadp_s4_criminal_provisions_subject/1,
    swiss_fadp_s4_criminal_provisions_profile_for/2,
    swiss_fadp_s4_criminal_provisions_assess/2
]).

:- use_module(ch/swiss_fadp_s4_criminal_provisions/swiss_fadp_s4_criminal_provisions, [decide_swiss_fadp_s4_criminal_provisions/2]).

% ---- Subject registry ------------------------------------------------
swiss_fadp_s4_criminal_provisions_subject(punishable_article_63).
